 * Portal-wide, PERSISTENT Matrix workspace.
 *
 * Mounted ONCE at the portal shell level (components/portal/Shell.tsx), exactly
 * like the terminal dock and the mail composer. Because the App Router keeps
 * Shell mounted across in-portal navigation, the whole Matrix subtree — every
 * open console, its per-console transcript/input state, and any live server
 * terminal websocket inside it — survives moving between dashboard pages. Leave
 * Matrix mid-build, wander the portal, come back, and it is exactly as you left
 * it (the sidebar "running"/"update" tag tells you when to come back).
 *
 * How it stays alive:
 *   - The workspace is rendered into a fixed panel that occupies the main
 *     content region ONLY while the route is /dashboard/build; on every other
 *     route the panel is `display:none` but STILL MOUNTED, so React never
 *     unmounts BuildStudio/BuildConsole and their sockets keep running.
 *   - It is lazy: nothing is fetched or mounted until the customer first opens
 *     Matrix (`activated` latches true), so users who never touch it pay nothing.
 *   - Data (servers, recent builds, key status) is re-fetched each time the
 *     route is entered and passed as fresh props. BuildStudio's console state
 *     lives in its own `useState` (initialised once), so refreshed props update
 *     the dropdowns/board without ever resetting the open consoles.
 *
 * The /dashboard/build PAGE is a thin placeholder — this panel covers it.
 */

